# Extracted full text of the Imagine rulebooks.
#
# Kept local, never committed. Permission to build and publish a Foundry conversion is not
# permission to republish the books themselves, and this repository is public -- committing
# them would put the complete text of commercial titles where anyone can read them.
#
# A PATTERN, not a list of the books we happened to have first. The four titles were named
# here one per line, so extracting a fifth -- the Master Index, Epitaph of the Fallen --
# silently produced a file that WAS NOT IGNORED and would have been committed by the next
# `git add -A`. Anything the extractor writes is book text and none of it is publishable.
#
# Regenerate from the PDFs when needed:
#     python tools/extract/extract_book_text.py <book.pdf> <name>
docs/reference/*-fulltext.txt

# Source PDFs, if they ever land inside the working tree.
*.pdf

# Python bytecode from the extraction tooling.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Per-developer Claude Code settings. The shared settings file is .claude/settings.json;
# the .local one holds one person's own permission grants and is not the project's business.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local test-server config: the port changes every run.
.claude/launch.json

# The built system zip IS committed, deliberately. It is what system.json's `download` points at,
# so Foundry can fetch an update itself: manifest and archive travel in the same commit and
# therefore can never disagree about what version is being offered. It is ~0.5 MB, which is a fair
# price for the update button working. Any OTHER zip in dist/ is still scratch.
dist/*.zip
!dist/imagine-rpg.zip
